    <title>Field Day 2027 Planning — AAR is live &amp; we want your ideas on GitHub</title>
  </head>
  <body>
    <p>M&amp;K Field Day Team —</p>
    <p>Thanks again to everyone who participated in our Field Day 2026 debrief meeting and contributed to what turned out to be a strong operation — over 50 years at Fort Flagler and still going strong. We learned a lot this year and captured some great ideas for 2027.</p>
    
    <p>The <strong>After Action Review (AAR)</strong> is now live and captures everything from our debrief discussion: speaker contributions, improvement ideas, and action items — all linked to tracked issues in our planning repository.</p>

    <h2>📄 Field Day 2026 After Action Review</h2>
    <div class="callout">
      <div class="link-block">
        <span class="label">AAR Document:</span><br>
        <a href="https://github.com/tsayles/field-day-2027/blob/main/docs/debrief/aar-mk-2026-field-day-discussion.md">M&amp;K Field Day 2026 — AAR Discussion (GitHub)</a>
      </div>
      <div class="link-block" style="margin-top:10px;">
        <span class="label">Pull Request (merged):</span><br>
        <a href="https://github.com/tsayles/field-day-2027/pull/29">PR #29 — Add M&amp;K Field Day 2026 After Action Review</a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p>The AAR covers the debrief discussion with summaries of each speaker's contributions, equipment issues (trailer damage, rotor failures), staffing challenges, and 9+ improvement ideas already converted to tracked issues.</p>

    <h2>🎯 Field Day 2027 Planning Project</h2>
    <p>We've launched a <strong>public GitHub project</strong> to coordinate planning for Field Day 2027. This is where we're tracking all improvement ideas, equipment repairs, logistics changes, and action items for next year's operation.</p>

    <div class="callout">
      <div class="link-block">
        <span class="label">Field Day 2027 Project Board (public):</span><br>
        <a href="https://github.com/users/tsayles/projects/5">https://github.com/users/tsayles/projects/5</a>
      </div>
      <div class="link-block" style="margin-top:10px;">
        <span class="label">GitHub Repository:</span><br>
        <a href="https://github.com/tsayles/field-day-2027">https://github.com/tsayles/field-day-2027</a>
      </div>
      <div class="link-block" style="margin-top:10px;">
        <span class="label">Issues (ideas &amp; action items):</span><br>
        <a href="https://github.com/tsayles/field-day-2027/issues">https://github.com/tsayles/field-day-2027/issues</a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p>Current tracked items include trailer repairs, antenna and rotor replacements, GOTA station improvements, staffing coordination, and more. There are already <strong>27+ improvement ideas</strong> from the FD 2026 debrief.</p>

    <h2>🙋 Get Involved — We Need Your Input</h2>
    <p>You don't need to be a developer to contribute — just a club member with ideas. Here's how you can help make Field Day 2027 even better:</p>

    <ul>
      <li><strong>Open an issue</strong> — share what worked, what didn't, or what you'd like to see next year. Short or long, all ideas welcome.</li>
      <li><strong>Comment on existing issues</strong> — add your thoughts, experiences, or suggestions to issues already being tracked.</li>
      <li><strong>Submit a pull request</strong> — got documentation, station notes, or procedural improvements? PRs welcome!</li>
      <li><strong>Browse the project board</strong> — see what's already being worked on and pick something to help with.</li>
    </ul>

    <p>If you're not already on GitHub, it's <strong>free to sign up</strong> and takes just a minute. Once you have an account you can comment on issues, open new ones, and help shape what we do differently next year.</p>

    <div class="note">
      <strong>New to GitHub?</strong> No problem. You can also <strong>reply directly to this email</strong> with your feedback, suggestions, or questions and I'll make sure they get captured in the project.
    </div>

    <h2>📋 What We're Working On</h2>
    <p>Some of the key areas for Field Day 2027 planning include:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Trailer damage assessment and repairs (<a href="https://github.com/tsayles/field-day-2027/issues/25">#25</a>, <a href="https://github.com/tsayles/field-day-2027/issues/26">#26</a>)</li>
      <li>Antenna and rotor maintenance/replacement</li>
      <li>GOTA station improvements and operator recruitment</li>
      <li>Station staffing coordination and volunteer sign-ups</li>
      <li>Digital station band planning and equipment configuration</li>
      <li>Radio Camp and pre-event training opportunities</li>
      <li>Procedural documentation and knowledge transfer</li>
    </ul>

    <p>Check the <a href="https://github.com/tsayles/field-day-2027/issues">issues list</a> for the full inventory of ideas and action items.</p>

    <h2>🗓️ Looking Ahead</h2>
    <p>Field Day 2027 will be held <strong>June 26–27, 2027</strong> (11:00 AM Saturday through 11:00 AM Sunday PDT), with Radio Camp starting Monday, June 21. We'll be back at Fort Flagler State Park continuing our 50+ year tradition.</p>

    <p>Thanks for everything you contributed to make Field Day 2026 a great event. With your continued input and involvement, we'll make 2027 even better!</p>

